Package: netRobust
Title: Network Robustness Under Random Failures and Targeted Attacks
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Manuel J.", "Zetina-Rejón", , "mzetina@ipn.mx", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7181-9828"))
Description: Simulates and compares network robustness to random node
    failures and targeted attacks (by degree, betweenness, closeness,
    eigenvector centrality, PageRank, and Kleinberg's HITS hub/authority
    scores), extending the approach of Albert, Jeong & Barabasi (2000)
    <doi:10.1038/35019019>. Includes a Monte Carlo framework for testing
    whether an attack scenario is statistically more damaging than random
    failure, and utilities for plotting robustness curves with a
    null-model reference envelope.
